FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: remove_digits
Signature: char remove_digits(big_int *digit, int N)
Description: /**
 * @brief Remove digits from a big integer starting at a specified position.
 *
 * Recursively traverses the linked list representing a big integer and frees
 * nodes from the Nth digit onward. If N is positive, it skips N digits before
 * starting removal; otherwise, it removes all remaining digits.
 *
 * @param digit Pointer to the current digit node in the big integer list.
 *              If NULL, the function returns immediately.
 * @param N     Number of leading digits to preserve. If N > 0, the first N
 *              digits are kept; if N <= 0, all remaining digits are removed.
 *
 * @return Always returns 0. A return of 0 indicates the function has completed,
 *         but does not signify success or failure of memory operations.
 *
 * @note Memory: Frees all digit nodes from position N onward. The caller's
 *       original pointer may become invalid if the head node is freed.
 * @note Recursion: Uses recursion for traversal; depth equals list length.
 */
Dependencies: remove_digits

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION (REFERENCE ONLY - do NOT copy into test):
```c
// C program for the function called remove_digits
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <time.h>

// Forward declarations for dependency functions

// Target function implementation
char remove_digits(big_int *digit, int N)
{
    if (digit == NULL)
        return 0;

    if (digit->next_digit == NULL)
    {
        free(digit);
        digit = NULL;
        return 0;
    }

    if (N > 0)
        return remove_digits(digit->next_digit, N - 1);

    return remove_digits(digit->next_digit, 0);
}

```

TARGET EXECUTION PATH:
Path 4: START | START --> CONDITION | if-else head --> STATEMENT | (digit == NULL) --> MERGE | if-else merge --> CONDITION | if-else head --> STATEMENT | (digit->next_digit == NULL) --> STATEMENT | free(digit); --> STATEMENT | digit = NULL; --> RETURN | return 0;

